 can  also get the sum of cubes formula from  this  we will make this substitution that y is  equal to negative z  we substitute this in and then we will  carefully simplify  the result will be the sum of cube's  formula  that x cubed plus z cubed is equal to  the factor x plus z multiplied by the  factor x squared minus x z plus z  squared  now let's solve the problem  1 divided by the cube root of 25 plus  the cube root of 5 plus 1  is equal to 1 divided by the cube root  of five squared plus the cube root of  five plus one  let x equal the cube root of five  the denominator then becomes x squared  plus x plus one  now this factor in the denominator is  reminiscent of the factor in the  difference of cubes  suppose y is equal to one  one factor becomes x squared plus x plus  one and the other factor is x minus one  the product of these two factors is  equal to x cubed minus one  if we substitute x is equal to the cube  root of five  then x cubed is equal to five  then five minus one is equal to four  from here we can see that we can  rationalize the denominator by  multiplying the numerator and  denominator by the factor x minus one  this is the rationalizing factor  the denominator then is equal to four  and the numerator is equal to x minus  one  so simplifying we get x minus one all  over four  we divide through by four to get one  fourth x minus one over four  then x is equal to the cube root of 5 so  we get 1 over 4 multiplied by the cube  root of 5 minus 1 over 4.  we now equate this to the original  equation a multiplied by the cube root  of 25 plus b multiplied by the cube root  of five plus c  we can then equate coefficients to get  that a is equal to zero  b is equal to one over four and c is  equal to negative one over four thus a  plus b plus c  is equal to zero  and that's the answer  i want to end the video with a little  bit of extra credit  suppose  one divided by the 4th root of 27  plus the 4th root of 9 plus the 4th root  of 3 plus 1  is equal t